{{!-- The Mode switch — light or dark. The `mode` Alpine store (assets/js/main.js) owns the `.dark`
class on <html> and its localStorage mirror; the pre-paint script in default.hbs has already resolved
which of the two it is before anything paints.

The label is therefore two spans and no JavaScript. It used to be one span server-rendered from
`default_appearance` and corrected by `x-text` once Alpine booted, which got the word wrong for every
visitor whose resolved Mode differed from the setting — always, with the setting on System and a dark
OS: the page painted dark under a button reading "Light". Letting the same class that decided the Mode
decide the word removes the disagreement, and keeps the label inside the theme's translate contract
instead of handing it to a hardcoded English string in a store getter. --}}
<button
	type="button"
	x-data
	x-bind:aria-pressed="$store.mode.dark"
	aria-pressed="false"
	aria-label="{{t "Toggle dark mode"}}"
	class="btn rounded-pill border-border bg-surface font-ui text-text flex cursor-pointer items-center gap-[9px] border px-4 py-2 text-[13px] font-medium shadow-sm hover:bg-surface-2"
	@click="$store.mode.toggle()">
	<span
		aria-hidden="true"
		class="bg-accent size-3 rounded-full"
		style="box-shadow: inset -4px 0 0 0 var(--mirror-dot-inset)"></span>
	<span class="dark:hidden">{{t "Light"}}</span><span class="hidden dark:inline">{{t "Dark"}}</span>
</button>
